T-005 blast-radius regression (revised, both runtimes): tests/loops/loop-inventory.json
and tests/lib/loop-driver.{sh,ps1} are cross-epic shared surfaces (Security
Boundary B2).

Correction over the prior coder-regression.log (this same directory): that log's
enumeration technique was 'grep -l loop-driver.sh tests/*.tests.sh' -- a .sh-only
glob that structurally cannot match a PowerShell suite, so no .ps1 consumer of the
modified tests/lib/loop-driver.ps1 was ever enumerated or run, and the .sh-side
enumeration itself also missed one real consumer (tests/hitl-wfi-terminal.tests.sh,
which sources tests/lib/loop-driver.sh at its own line 44 but does not match a
plain-substring grep restricted to files literally named tests/*.tests.sh -- it
does, so the omission there was incompleteness of the original run, not a glob
defect; corrected here regardless).

Revised technique: grep -lE 'loop-driver\.(sh|ps1)' across both tests/*.tests.sh AND
tests/*.tests.ps1, then each match manually inspected to confirm it is a genuine
'. (dot-source)' of tests/lib/loop-driver.{sh,ps1} (never a comment mention).

Genuine consumers, both runtimes (5 each): tests/hitl-wfi-terminal.tests.{sh,ps1},
tests/loop-consistency.tests.{sh,ps1}, tests/loop-driver.tests.{sh,ps1},
tests/loop-escalation.tests.{sh,ps1}, tests/loop-inventory.tests.{sh,ps1}.

run-all.sh/.ps1 is still not used here for the same reason as the prior log:
this repository's own deterministic-lane self-check fails closed until a human
applies the staged human-copy CI patch (precedent: T-004's own
qg-cycle2/T-004/regression.log).

